[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: TC-H1FWHVPSIB-
TITLE: Test Protocol

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPSIB-5
TITLE: Functional 1 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall jump to execution of the HVPS interface application
if and only if the existing application code at startup is valid. The application code is valid if the
programmed CRC value matches the application firmware loaded in flash memory.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is ready to start.
* Flash memory is present which contains firmware application.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system from power.
2. Do not load any treatment plan.
3. Utilize the bootloader utility to load a new set of application firmware from the flash memory, but partway through, terminate the PC utility.
4. Power cycle the system.
5. Load a treatment plan.
6. Run the loaded treatment.
7. While keeping power on, load the application firmware once more through to completion from the flash memory.
8. Power cycle the system.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify system starts up successfully.
2. Verify system does not have any treatment plan loaded on it.
3. Verify the system is off.
4. Verify system starts up successfully.
5. Verify the plan is loaded successfully.
6. Verify the treatment plan cannot be executed.
7. Verify the application is loaded successfully.
8. Verify the system powered up successfully and the loaded treatment can now be performed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-1
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPSIB-6
TITLE: Functional 2 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall write application data provided by the PC through
application-relative page index 180.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is ready to start.
* A bootloader-compatible application image contains known, non-erased data at application-relative
  page index 180.
* A flash inspection tool is available to read the programmed application memory.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system from power.
2. Do not load any treatment plan.
3. Utilize the bootloader utility to load the prepared application firmware image.
4. Record the utility log for the write to application-relative page index 180.
5. Read back application-relative page index 180 with the flash inspection tool.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify system starts up successfully.
2. Verify system does not have any treatment plan loaded on it.
3. Verify the bootloader utility completes the application load without rejecting page index 180.
4. Verify the utility log reports that page index 180 was written successfully.
5. Verify the read-back data at page index 180 matches the prepared application image.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-2
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPSIB-7
TITLE: Functional 3 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall be able to erase a predetermined area of flash
memory, corresponding to the application firmware programming area.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is ready to start in bootloader mode.
* The application programming area contains known, non-erased marker data in its first page and at
  application-relative page index 180.
* A protocol-compatible tool can send an erase command and inspect MCU flash memory.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system from power in bootloader mode.
2. Use the protocol-compatible tool to send an erase command.
3. Record the bootloader response.
4. Read back the marker locations in the first application page and at application-relative page
   index 180.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify system starts up successfully in bootloader mode.
2. Verify the bootloader reports that the erase completed.
3. Verify the erase response is received before inspecting flash.
4. Verify both marker locations contain the erased flash value.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-3
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPSIB-8
TITLE: PC Communication - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall be able to respond to a ping command from the PC,
indicating that the system is in bootloader mode.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is ready to start.
* Flash memory is present which contains firmware application.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system from power.
2. Do not load any treatment plan.
3. Utilize the bootloader utility to load a new set of application firmware from the flash memory.
4. Record the utility log to ensure application enters bootloader mode.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify system starts up successfully.
2. Verify system does not have any treatment plan loaded on it.
3. Verify the new firmware application is loaded successfully.
4. Verify application enters bootloader mode.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-4
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPSIB-9
TITLE: MCUboot Image Validation - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall validate application images using the MCUboot bootutil
library with EC256 signature verification.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is ready to start.
* A valid application image with correct EC256 signature is available.
* An invalid application image with incorrect signature is available.
* An application image with corrupted header is available.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power cycle the system with valid application image in flash.
2. Verify bootloader validates and jumps to application.
3. Power cycle the system with invalid signature image.
4. Verify bootloader rejects the image and enters bootloader mode.
5. Power cycle the system with corrupted header image.
6. Verify bootloader rejects the image and enters bootloader mode.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Bootloader validates image successfully.
2. Application jumps and runs normally.
3. Bootloader validates signature and rejects invalid image.
4. Bootloader displays appropriate error and waits for commands.
5. Bootloader validates header and rejects corrupted image.
6. Bootloader displays appropriate error and enters bootloader mode.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-5
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPSIB-10
TITLE: Stack Pointer Validation - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall validate that the stack pointer from the application
vector table is within the valid RAM range.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is ready to start.
* A valid application image with correct stack pointer is available.
* A modified application image with stack pointer below valid range (0x20000000) is available.
* A modified application image with stack pointer above valid range (0x20008000) is available.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power cycle with valid stack pointer application.
2. Verify application jumps and runs normally.
3. Power cycle with stack pointer below range (e.g., 0x1FFFFFFF).
4. Verify bootloader rejects the image and displays ERR_SP error.
5. Power cycle with stack pointer above range (e.g., 0x20009000).
6. Verify bootloader rejects the image and displays ERR_SP error.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Bootloader reads valid stack pointer from vector table.
2. Bootloader validates it is within 0x20000000 to 0x20008000 and jumps to application.
3. Bootloader reads invalid stack pointer.
4. Bootloader validates and rejects due to out-of-range value, outputs "ERR_SP\n".
5. Bootloader reads invalid stack pointer.
6. Bootloader validates and rejects due to out-of-range value, outputs "ERR_SP\n".
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-6
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPSIB-11
TITLE: Reset Handler Validation - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall validate that the reset handler address from the
application vector table is within the valid application code range.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is ready to start.
* A valid application image with correct reset handler is available.
* A modified application image with reset handler pointing to bootloader space is available.
* A modified application image with reset handler above application slot limit is available.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power cycle with valid reset handler application.
2. Verify application jumps and runs normally.
3. Power cycle with reset handler in bootloader region (e.g., 0x08000000).
4. Verify bootloader rejects the image and displays ERR_RH error.
5. Power cycle with reset handler beyond application limit (e.g., 0x08025000).
6. Verify bootloader rejects the image and displays ERR_RH error.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Bootloader reads valid reset handler from vector table.
2. Bootloader validates it is within application range and jumps to application.
3. Bootloader reads invalid reset handler in bootloader space.
4. Bootloader validates and rejects due to out-of-range value, outputs "ERR_RH\n".
5. Bootloader reads invalid reset handler beyond slot.
6. Bootloader validates and rejects due to out-of-range value, outputs "ERR_RH\n".
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-7
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPSIB-12
TITLE: Image Address Validation - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS interface bootloader firmware shall validate that the application image start address is
within the valid application slot range.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is ready to start.
* A valid application image is located at the correct start address.
* An application image with start address below valid range is available.
* An application image with start address above valid range is available.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power cycle with application at valid start address (0x0800C200).
2. Verify bootloader validates and jumps to application.
3. Power cycle with application start address at 0x0800B000 (below valid range).
4. Verify bootloader rejects the image and displays ERR_ADDR error.
5. Power cycle with application start address at 0x08025000 (above valid range).
6. Verify bootloader rejects the image and displays ERR_ADDR error.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Bootloader calculates image start from MCUboot header.
2. Bootloader validates address is between 0x0800C200 and 0x08024000 and jumps to application.
3. Bootloader detects invalid start address below range.
4. Bootloader outputs "ERR_ADDR\n" and remains in bootloader mode.
5. Bootloader detects invalid start address above range.
6. Bootloader outputs "ERR_ADDR\n" and remains in bootloader mode.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-8
  ROLE: Verifies

[[/SECTION]]
